## Guard empty and non-numeric input where it is converted
`float("")` and `int("12a")` raise ValueError, which ends the program when nothing expects it at the conversion point.
```python
# bad
weight_kg = float(input("Weight (kg): "))
```
```python
# good
def parse_weight(raw):
    text = raw.strip()
    if text == "":
        raise ValueError("Enter a weight.")
    try:
        return float(text)
    except ValueError:
        raise ValueError(f"Weight must be a number, got {text!r}.") from None
```
